[2.6.4]
* Update NetBird server and the optional reverse proxy from 0.81.4 to 0.81.5 with pinned image digests.
* Keep dashboard v2.95.0 and Cloudron base 6.0.1. No configuration changes. Upstream SSH session validation and queue bounds are client-side fixes; update clients separately to receive them.

[2.6.3]
* Update NetBird server and the optional reverse proxy from 0.81.3 to 0.81.4, including the upstream fix to distrust compromised eMudhra CA keys.
* Keep dashboard v2.95.0 and Cloudron base 6.0.1. No configuration changes. The upstream SSH privilege-dropping fix is client-side and requires updating clients separately.

[2.6.2]
* Update NetBird server and the optional reverse proxy from 0.81.2 to 0.81.3, including the upstream relay QUIC dependency update.
* Update the dashboard from v2.94.0 to v2.95.0. It adds the certificate posture check editor for NetBird 0.81, per-target HTTP access controls for reverse-proxy services, duplicating policies, and peer search by MAC address. Search engines are now blocked by default via robots.txt.
* Optional second-IP reverse-proxy ingress: the host helper now restores its firewall guard before readiness checks, so a failed check after a reboot keeps the backend port blocked instead of reachable. Copy the released scripts/netbird-ingress.py to /etc/netbird-ingress/ on hosts that use it; an app update alone does not change it.
* Update the Cloudron base image from 6.0.0 to 6.0.1. No configuration changes.

[2.6.1]
* Update NetBird server and the optional reverse proxy from 0.80.0 to 0.81.2. NetBird 0.81 adds certificate posture checks (peers must hold a device certificate from your own CA; needs clients 0.81.0 or newer, not available on iOS or Android).
* The dashboard stays at v2.94.0, so new 0.81 options that need a newer dashboard are not shown yet. No configuration changes.

[2.6.0]
* New installs with Cloudron SSO: creating the owner account at /setup also adds Cloudron as a login option. New Cloudron users need owner approval, and the owner login stays as the recovery login. If adding it fails, setup still works and the log explains the manual steps. Existing installs are unaffected.
* The dashboard's Add Peer command now includes --enable-rosenpass --rosenpass-permissive, so new devices get post-quantum tunnels without losing connections to devices that don't have Rosenpass. Set NETBIRD_CLIENT_ROSENPASS to strict or off to change it.

[2.5.0]
* The native client port now accepts only post-quantum TLS 1.3 (X25519MLKEM768), so recorded client traffic can't be decrypted later by a quantum computer. NetBird clients older than 0.61.0 can no longer connect unless you set the NETBIRD_TLS_ALLOW_CLASSIC=true app environment variable.
* Setup instructions now include --enable-rosenpass for post-quantum device tunnels. See docs/POST-QUANTUM.md for migrating existing devices and auditing them.

[2.4.4]
* Monitoring guide: also check that the proxy backend port is closed over IPv6. The app image is unchanged.

[2.4.3]
* Fix IPv6 detection so the IPv6 native client listener from 2.4.2 is actually enabled on IPv6-enabled servers.

[2.4.2]
* Native NetBird clients can now connect over IPv6 on IPv6-enabled servers; previously only IPv4 worked.
* Add an external monitoring guide with a recommended updown.io check plan for the app, native port and optional proxy.

[2.4.1]
* Optional reverse-proxy host helper: restore the public ingress and backend port guard automatically after a server reboot.
* The ingress check timer now restarts a failed ingress or bridge service instead of reporting success. Replace the host helper file to apply; the app image is unchanged.

[2.4.0]
* Use Cloudron's platform STUN service by default; new installs no longer need a dedicated STUN UDP port.
* Make the dedicated STUN port optional; existing installs keep their binding and NetBird's own STUN server.
* Keep NetBird's built-in relay for peers that cannot connect directly; Cloudron's TURN relay and secret are not used.
* Trust forwarded client addresses only from the in-container proxies.
* Update to Cloudron base 6.0.0 and dashboard v2.94.0.

[2.3.1]
* Update the combined NetBird server and optional reverse proxy to v0.80.0 with immutable image digests.
* Retain dashboard v2.93.0 and the pinned Cloudron base 5.1.0; no automatic proxy or SSO configuration changes.

[2.3.0]
* Add opt-in operator reconciliation of Cloudron user/group app access to NetBird SSO-user approval and blocking.
* Preserve embedded recovery owners, existing peer ownership, other providers and user roles/groups.
* Retain immutable identity bindings and pending revocation recovery state; default to a non-mutating plan.
* Move operator guides under docs/ and document native Cloudron VPN-provider limitations.
* No automatic synchronization service or peer migration is enabled by an app update.

[2.2.0]
* Include optional Cloudron OIDC addon onboarding for new installs.
* Add owner-operated SSO switching for existing installs without database flag edits or peer migration.
* Preserve client/connector identities, embedded recovery login and new-user approval across toggles.
* Add scoped public-ingress connection limits, managed denylist, protection rollback and reporting.

[2.1.0]
* Add opt-in bundled NetBird Reverse Proxy with dedicated-IP host TLS forwarding.
* Keep proxy disabled by default and preserve normal Cloudron dashboard/native-client traffic.
* Add local-only initial setup, proxy credential/certificate persistence, and live peer-to-service verification.

